{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7c1a2d4-0f36-4c58-9e21-6a1d3f5c8e10",
    "name": "Ownspce API",
    "description": "Zero-knowledge sync API for Ownspce.\n\nThe server stores and moves **ciphertext only**. Tier 0 identity and membership data lives in real columns; Tier 1 workspace documents and Tier 2 change logs are opaque sealed blobs the server can never decrypt.\n\n## Getting a session\n\n`POST /auth/session` needs a real Google or Apple ID token, which only a signed-in app can produce. Once you run it, the collection captures `accessToken`, `refreshToken`, `deviceId`, and `userId` automatically; `POST /spaces` captures `spaceId`, and the sync poll captures `sinceCursor`. Everything after that just works.\n\nNo ID token handy? Mint an access token for a test user with `go run ./cmd/e2e` in the repo, or paste one into the `accessToken` collection variable.\n\n## About the sample payloads\n\n`{{sampleCiphertext}}`, `{{sampleSnapshot}}`, `{{sampleWrappedKey}}`, and `{{samplePublicKey}}` are random bytes of the **correct length**, generated fresh before each request. They exercise the API's shape validation, not real encryption — a real client encrypts on-device with XChaCha20-Poly1305 after padding to a bucket. See `docs/client-crypto.md`.\n\nSealed payloads must be exactly `bucket + 40` bytes (24B nonce + 16B tag), where bucket ∈ 1024, 4096, 16384, 65536, 262144. Anything else is rejected with `413 bucket_violation`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Fresh sample crypto material for every request. Correct lengths, random",
          "// bytes — enough to exercise shape validation, not real ciphertext.",
          "const crypto = require('crypto-js');",
          "const randomB64 = (byteCount) =>",
          "  crypto.lib.WordArray.random(byteCount).toString(crypto.enc.Base64);",
          "",
          "const AEAD_OVERHEAD = 40; // 24B nonce + 16B Poly1305 tag",
          "",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set('samplePublicKey', randomB64(32));",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set('sampleWrappedKey', randomB64(80));",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set('sampleCiphertext', randomB64(1024 + AEAD_OVERHEAD));",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set('sampleSnapshot', randomB64(4096 + AEAD_OVERHEAD));"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Every endpoint returns JSON, and errors always carry a machine-readable code.",
          "if (pm.response.code !== 204 && pm.response.code !== 304) {",
          "  pm.test('response is json', () => pm.response.to.be.json);",
          "}",
          "if (pm.response.code >= 400) {",
          "  pm.test('error has a code', () =>",
          "    pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.have.nested.property('error.code'));",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
